# Cursor Configuration for LY-UI Documentation

## Documentation Structure Rules

### MDX Documentation Format
- All component documentation must follow this structure:
  1. **Header** (title, description)
  2. **Preview** (single component with basic props)
  3. **Example** (complete usage with callbacks)
  4. **Documentation** (props table)
  5. **Features** (capabilities list)

### Preview Section Rules
- Use only ONE component instance in preview
- NO callbacks in preview props (causes client component errors)
- Include basic props with realistic English data
- Use `className="w-full max-w-md"` for responsive sizing
- Import component at top: `import ComponentName from '@/components/LY UI/AI/componentName'`

### Example Section Rules
- Include complete usage with all callbacks
- Use realistic English examples
- Show state management with `useState`
- Include error handling and logging
- Demonstrate multiple use cases

### Documentation Table Rules
- Include ALL actual props from component source
- NO fictional props - only real component props
- Include Type, Default, and Description for each prop
- Use proper TypeScript types
- Add Types section for complex types

### Features Section Rules
- List 6-8 key capabilities
- Use bullet points with bold feature names
- Focus on user benefits and technical capabilities
- Include accessibility and responsive design

## Component Documentation Standards

### Import Statements
```tsx
import ComponentName from '@/components/LY UI/AI/componentName'
```

### Preview Format
```tsx
<Preview link="componentName">
  <ComponentName 
    prop1="realistic value"
    prop2={realisticValue}
    className="w-full max-w-md"
  />
</Preview>
```

### Example Format
```tsx
export default function ComponentExample() {
  const handleCallback = () => {
    console.log('Callback executed')
  }

  return (
    <ComponentName
      prop1="value"
      prop2={value}
      onCallback={handleCallback}
      className="w-full max-w-md"
    />
  )
}
```

### Documentation Table Format
| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `propName` | `Type` | `default` | Clear description |

## Language and Content Rules

### English Only
- All documentation must be in English
- Use professional, clear language
- Maintain consistent terminology
- Use American English spelling

### Realistic Examples
- Use realistic but fictional data
- Include proper error handling
- Show practical use cases
- Demonstrate best practices

### Accessibility Focus
- Always mention screen reader support
- Include keyboard navigation details
- Highlight responsive design
- Emphasize user experience

## File Organization

### Naming Convention
- Use PascalCase for component names
- Use kebab-case for file names
- Match component name in file name

### Directory Structure
```
content/docs/components/AI/
├── componentName.mdx
├── anotherComponent.mdx
└── ...
```

## Code Quality Standards

### TypeScript
- Use proper TypeScript types
- Include type definitions when needed
- Use strict typing for props

### React Best Practices
- Use functional components
- Include proper prop validation
- Follow React hooks patterns
- Use modern React patterns

### Performance
- Mention performance considerations
- Include optimization tips
- Highlight efficient usage patterns

## Documentation Maintenance

### Update Process
1. Read component source file first
2. Extract actual props and types
3. Create realistic examples
4. Test preview functionality
5. Verify all links work

### Quality Checklist
- [ ] All props documented
- [ ] No fictional props
- [ ] Realistic examples
- [ ] Proper TypeScript types
- [ ] Accessibility mentioned
- [ ] Responsive design noted
- [ ] English language used
- [ ] Professional tone maintained

## Error Prevention

### Common Issues to Avoid
- Don't include callbacks in preview props
- Don't create fictional component props
- Don't use French in documentation
- Don't skip accessibility features
- Don't forget responsive design
- Don't use inconsistent naming

### Validation Rules
- Preview must render without errors
- All imports must be correct
- Props must match component source
- Examples must be functional
- Links must be valid

## Special Instructions

### AI Components Focus
- Emphasize AI/ML capabilities
- Include real-time features
- Highlight interactive elements
- Show progressive animations
- Demonstrate state management

### User Experience Priority
- Focus on developer experience
- Include clear usage examples
- Provide practical scenarios
- Show integration patterns
- Highlight customization options 